meta {
  name: Retry ingest
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/books/{{bookId}}/retry
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 409
}

tests {
  test("refuses a book that did not fail", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(409);
  });
}

docs {
  **Expected to return 409 here, and that is the point.**

  Retry only accepts a book in `failed` state. Re-running one that is mid-ingest would
  put two workers on the same book, and the task is idempotent against a retry of itself
  — not against a second concurrent run.

  To exercise the 202 path, force a failure first:

  ```sql
  update public.books set status = 'failed', error = 'forced' where id = '<bookId>';
  ```
}
